      "content": "Yes, soil health is as vital as nutrient balance, and fungal diseases like brown patch or grubs can severely hamper nitrogen absorption even if the soil looks perfect. You should also snip a small section of turf to check for thatch buildup, which can block fertilizer from reaching the roots and leaving the grass looking greasy instead of green. Additionally, using a pre-emergent herbicide at the wrong time can create a barrier that prevents nutrients from being taken up correctly. Choosing the right fertilizer and then doing a deep inspection of the plant roots and soil surface can rule out these biological and physical blockages before they make the recovery process much longer.",
